{
  "_comment": [
    "A deliberately small, HAND-WRITTEN stand-in for the /sceneweaver/fields",
    "payload and for the widget lists ComfyUI builds from define_schema().",
    "",
    "Hand-written rather than generated on purpose. A generated fixture would",
    "have to import the data layer, and importing it runs the user_options.json",
    "merge -- which would bake whichever pool values the maintainer happened to",
    "have locally into a committed file (the failure named in the memory lesson",
    "'feedback-generator-cannot-leak-user-data'). It would also be ~130KB of",
    "pool values to prove behaviour that eight fields prove just as well.",
    "",
    "What stops it drifting from the real payload is not a --check on this file",
    "but tests/test_frontend_payload.py, which asserts the real pack produces",
    "the same STRUCTURE this declares -- the direction that actually matters,",
    "since the frontend reads a shape and Python must keep emitting it.",
    "",
    "The genre here is fictional ('fixture'), which is also a small proof that",
    "js/sceneweaver.js knows nothing about sci-fi: it is handed node ids and",
    "field data, never a genre."
  ],
